---
import ServicePageLayout from '../../layouts/ServicePageLayout.astro';

const data = {
  metaTitle: 'Web & Mobile App Development Australia | AWLabs',
  metaDescription: 'Web and mobile app development for Australian organisations: customer portals, internal tools and digital products that perform well on every device.',
  category: 'Development',
  serviceName: 'Web and Mobile App Development',
  heroHeadline: 'Web and Mobile Applications That Scale With Your Business',
  heroTagline: 'From customer portals to internal tools, performant, accessible and production-grade from launch day.',
  summaryStatement: 'Web and mobile app development is the building of applications that run in a browser, on iOS and Android, or both, such as customer portals, internal tools and digital products, usually sharing one backend and designed to perform on the devices people actually use.',
  description: [
    'The gap between a web application that merely works and one that drives measurable business outcomes is not a feature list, it is quality of execution. Slow page loads cost you customers. Mobile applications that crash under poor network conditions destroy trust faster than any marketing can rebuild it. Every application we deliver is engineered to the production standards your users expect and your infrastructure needs to support: Core Web Vitals in the green, accessibility built to WCAG 2.2 AA, and architecture that degrades gracefully under load rather than falling over.',
    'We build web applications using React and Next.js for consumer-grade interfaces, and pair them with robust Node.js or Go backends designed for high concurrency. Our mobile applications are built in Flutter for maximum code reuse across iOS and Android, or in React Native where team familiarity justifies the choice. We do not prescribe a stack, we recommend based on your team\'s long-term ownership requirements, your user base\'s device distribution, and the performance characteristics your use case demands. You get a considered recommendation with clear reasoning, not a default selection.',
  ],
  benefits: [
    {
      icon: '<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z"/></svg>',
      title: 'Sub-Second Performance Targets',
      description: 'Core Web Vitals are a first-class engineering requirement, not a post-launch audit. We implement server-side rendering, incremental static regeneration, code splitting and aggressive caching strategies to achieve LCP under 2.5s and CLS below 0.1 on real devices, not just Lighthouse.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2a10 10 0 1 0 0 20 10 10 0 0 0 0-20z"/><path d="M2 12h20M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z"/></svg>',
      title: 'WCAG 2.2 AA Accessibility',
      description: 'The Disability Discrimination Act applies to digital services, and WCAG 2.2 AA is the standard most often used to show accessibility. We build to WCAG 2.2 AA from the first commit: semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, screen reader testing with NVDA and VoiceOver, and colour contrast validation.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="5" y="2" width="14" height="20" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="12" y1="18" x2="12.01" y2="18"/></svg>',
      title: 'Mobile-First Without Compromise',
      description: 'Much of your audience will reach you on a phone. We design and test on real devices, not just browser emulators, covering the range of Android hardware our users actually carry, including mid-range devices where performance issues surface first.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3"/><path d="M21 12c0 1.66-4 3-9 3s-9-1.34-9-3"/><path d="M3 5v14c0 1.66 4 3 9 3s9-1.34 9-3V5"/></svg>',
      title: 'Data Architecture That Grows With You',
      description: 'Schema design, indexing strategy, and read/write separation are decisions made at project start, not during an incident at 2am when query times spike. We model data access patterns before writing migrations and build for the volume you will have in three years, not just today.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 15s1-1 4-1 5 2 8 2 4-1 4-1V3s-1 1-4 1-5-2-8-2-4 1-4 1z"/><line x1="4" y1="22" x2="4" y2="15"/></svg>',
      title: 'Instrumented From Day One',
      description: 'Error tracking via Sentry, real user monitoring via Datadog RUM, and structured logging piped into your observability stack of choice. We include a production monitoring runbook so your team knows exactly which alerts matter and what to do when they fire.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16z"/></svg>',
      title: 'Progressive Enhancement & Offline Support',
      description: 'For applications used in field environments or by users on unreliable connections, we implement service workers, local-first data sync with conflict resolution, and background sync APIs, so the application remains functional whether the user has full 5G or patchy regional 4G.',
    },
  ],
  /* useCases array emptied, previous content was fabricated; specific metrics (% improvements, throughput figures, deflection rates, NPS deltas) were not verifiable. Will return as honest capability statements once real, signed-off project examples can be referenced. */
  useCases: [],
  technologies: [
    'React', 'Next.js', 'TypeScript', 'Tailwind CSS', 'Node.js', 'GraphQL',
    'PostgreSQL', 'Redis', 'Flutter', 'React Native', 'Vercel', 'AWS',
  ],
  process: [
    {
      step: '01',
      title: 'Discovery Audit & Strategy Sessions',
      duration: 'Before the build',
      description: 'Every build starts with a Discovery Audit ($750 plus GST, credited in full against the build). We map user journeys, define performance benchmarks, look at any existing systems being replaced and set out the integrations. After two strategy sessions you receive a technology recommendation with reasons and a fixed price for an agreed scope.',
    },
    {
      step: '02',
      title: 'Design System & UX Foundations',
      duration: 'Weeks 2 to 5',
      description: 'We establish design tokens, component library, typography scale and accessibility patterns before building any screens. This investment pays back throughout the project, component-based design eliminates inconsistency and accelerates development velocity.',
    },
    {
      step: '03',
      title: 'Backend API & Data Layer',
      duration: 'Weeks 3 to 8',
      description: 'We design and build the API layer in parallel with UI work. API contracts are defined and shared early so frontend and backend development can proceed concurrently. Database schema, migration strategy and seed data are agreed before the first line of business logic is written.',
    },
    {
      step: '04',
      title: 'Frontend Build & Integration',
      duration: 'Weeks 5 to 16',
      description: 'Frontend development against the design system and API contracts. Sprint length is set for each build. You get an update every Tuesday and Friday, Sydney time, with access to test the latest work. Each stage delivers tested functionality for you to accept. Integrations with third-party services and internal systems are built progressively against stub responses first, then against real endpoints as they become available.',
    },
    {
      step: '05',
      title: 'Performance & Accessibility Audit',
      duration: '1 week pre-launch',
      description: 'Dedicated time for performance profiling, accessibility testing with assistive technologies, cross-browser validation on the target browser matrix, and load testing against the projected user concurrency. Issues are remediated before any launch date is committed to.',
    },
    {
      step: '06',
      title: 'Launch & 30 Day Warranty',
      duration: 'Launch + 30 days',
      description: 'Staged rollout with monitoring dashboards active from the moment production traffic begins. Error rates, performance metrics and user feedback are reviewed daily in the first two weeks. A 30 day warranty runs from launch: we fix bugs and anything caused by our work at no cost.',
    },
  ],
  industries: [
    'Financial Services & Superannuation',
    'Government & Utilities',
    'Property & Construction',
    'Healthcare',
    'Logistics & Supply Chain',
    'Professional Services',
    'Retail & eCommerce',
    'Education & Training',
  ],
  faqs: [
    {
      question: 'What is the difference between this service and custom app development?',
      answer: 'Custom App Development refers to purpose-built enterprise software that replaces or augments core business systems, think loan origination platforms, permit management systems, or complex operational tools. Web & Mobile Applications is broader and encompasses customer-facing products, internal productivity tools, portals and digital experiences where the focus is equally on user experience quality, front-end performance, and omnichannel delivery. In practice, a build often draws from both services. We scope based on what you are building and recommend the right approach for the complexity involved.',
    },
    {
      question: 'How do you decide between a web app, native mobile app, or cross-platform approach?',
      answer: 'The decision depends on four factors: the distribution of your user base across device types, the performance and hardware requirements of the application, the ongoing maintenance capacity of your team, and your go-to-market timeline. For most enterprise internal tools and B2B products, a responsive web application or a Flutter cross-platform app gives you the best return. Native iOS and Android development is warranted when you need deep hardware access (camera, AR, Bluetooth LE) or when App Store distribution to consumers is a primary acquisition channel. You get a specific recommendation with clear trade offs as part of your Discovery Audit.',
    },
    {
      question: 'How do you ensure the application performs well on older or mid-range devices?',
      answer: 'We define a minimum device support matrix at project start based on your actual user data or the Australian market distribution if you are launching a new product. Performance budgets are set for this baseline device, not the latest flagship hardware. We test on physical Android devices including mid-range Samsung and Oppo handsets, and use Chrome DevTools throttling to simulate 4G and 3G conditions during development, not just as a final check. Bundle size is monitored through automated CI checks, and any PR that inflates the bundle beyond a threshold requires justification.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Can the application integrate with our existing enterprise systems?',
      answer: 'Integration is a standard component of every application we build. We integrate with platforms such as SAP, Salesforce, Microsoft Dynamics, ServiceNow, Workday and Xero through their supported APIs. Where APIs do not exist, we design and build middleware layers with appropriate queuing, retry logic, and circuit breakers to maintain application resilience when upstream systems are degraded or unreachable.',
    },
    {
      question: 'What does ongoing support look like after the application launches?',
      answer: 'Every build includes a 30 day warranty from the day it goes live. In that time we fix bugs and any issue caused by our work at no cost. After that, ongoing support is available through a Care Plan: month to month, priced for your system. Support runs in New South Wales business hours with agreed response targets. After hours cover can be added where your system needs it. If you would rather hand the application to an internal team, our documentation is written for that, and we are available for new features later. We design applications to be maintainable by teams who were not involved in the original build.',
    },
    {
      question: 'How do you handle application security for customer-facing products?',
      answer: 'Customer-facing applications introduce a broader attack surface than internal tools. Our standard security posture includes OWASP Top 10 protections built into the application layer, rate limiting and bot detection at the edge, HTTPS enforcement with HSTS preloading, CSP headers, sub-resource integrity for third-party scripts, and regular automated dependency scanning via Dependabot or Snyk. For applications handling payment data, we keep card data out of your application by delegating it to Stripe or Windcave, which keeps your PCI DSS scope small. Security is tested throughout the build, including automated penetration testing before launch. If you want an independent penetration test by a specialist firm, we will help you arrange it.',
    },
    {
      question: 'What is the difference between a web app and a mobile app?',
      answer: 'A web app runs in a browser and works on any device without installation; a mobile app is installed from the App Store or Google Play and can use device features such as push notifications, the camera and offline storage more fully. Many products start as a responsive web app and add a mobile app, often built with Flutter, once usage justifies it.',
    },
    {
      question: 'How much does web and mobile app development cost?',
      answer: 'The main drivers are the number of screens and user roles, integrations with your existing systems, whether you need web, mobile or both, and security requirements. Every build is priced on its own scope. It starts with a Discovery Audit ($750 plus GST, credited in full against the build). After the audit you get a fixed price for an agreed scope, paid in three stages against work you have accepted. We never publish day rates. Our app development cost guide sets out typical Australian market ranges.',
    },
  ],
  relatedServices: [
    { title: 'Custom App Development', href: '/services/custom-app-development' },
    { title: 'Flutter Development', href: '/services/flutter-development' },
    { title: 'UI & UX Design', href: '/services/ui-ux-design' },
    { title: 'Cloud Infrastructure & DevOps', href: '/services/cloud-infrastructure' },
  ],
  heroIcon: '<svg width="120" height="120" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"/><rect x="5" y="7" width="5" height="4" rx="1"/><line x1="14" y1="9" x2="17" y2="9"/><line x1="14" y1="12" x2="17" y2="12"/></svg>',
};
---
<ServicePageLayout {...data} />
